Icon artwork is derived from the upstream sets below, each redistributed under
its own licence. A name carries a two-letter set code only where two sets draw
the same name, so a name does not reliably say which set a drawing came from;
the notices here cover the catalogue as a whole, and the source.json beside each
drawing names its set individually.

  Phosphor Icons, Copyright (c) 2023 Phosphor Icons
  https://github.com/phosphor-icons/core — MIT License

  Tabler Icons, Copyright (c) 2020-2024 Paweł Kuna
  https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons — MIT License

  Lucide, Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by Cole Bemis
  2013-2022 as part of Feather (MIT). All other copyright (c) for Lucide are
  held by Lucide Contributors 2022.
  https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide — ISC License

  Ionicons, Copyright (c) 2015-present Ionic (http://ionic.io/)
  https://github.com/ionic-team/ionicons — MIT License

Imported artwork is rescaled onto this library's 256-unit grid; the geometry is
otherwise unmodified. Tabler and Lucide are stroked drawings, stored as
centerline path data from which every weight is derived. Phosphor ships six
drawn weights and is stored as filled artwork, one file per weight. Ionicons
ships no lighter or heavier variant, so each of its icons carries one weight and
every other weight renders that one. LICENSES/
holds the full text of each licence above, one file per set, each a verbatim
copy of the LICENSE file in the upstream repository linked above.

Ionicons contributes its outline set and the 90 `logo-*` brand logos. The logos
were extracted from the Ionicons TrueType font as shipped in @expo/vector-icons,
which does not vendor Ionicons' own licence file, so LICENSES/ionicons.txt is
taken from the Ionicons repository itself rather than from that package.

Brand logos reproduce third-party trademarks. The drawings are Ionicons' and
travel under Ionicons' MIT terms; the marks they depict are not. Their owners'
trademark rights are not licensed by those terms or by this licence, and use
must not imply endorsement by or affiliation with the trademark owner.

